        "orario": "11:41",
        "timestamp": 1775641268,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. US, Israel and Iran agree to 2-week ceasefire as Trump pulls back on threats Issued on: 08/04/2026 - 11:41 Iran, the United States and Israel reached a two-week ceasefire Wednesday as U.S. President Donald Trump pulled back from his threats to destroy Iranian civilisation. The agreement came just hours before Trump's deadline for Iran to reopen the Strait of Hormuz or face attacks on its bridges and powerplants. US-Iran ceasefire ‘a major problem domestically’ for Netanyahu 08/04/2026 Middle East Iran portraying ceasefire as 'victory against the United States and Israel' 08/04/2026 Middle East EU farm fraud scandal rocks Greek government, PM urges swift action 07/04/2026 Europe NASA–ESA partnership: Artemis II paves way for exploring Moon’s far side and south pole 07/04/2026 Science Iran positively reviewing Pakistan’s request for a two-week ceasefire, source says 07/04/2026 Middle East Trump's 'rhetoric itself could create a norm' for others to terrorise entire populations 07/04/2026 Middle East An 'eerie still' in Tehran amid Trump's apocalyptic threats 07/04/2026 Middle East Kanye West refused entry to UK, Wireless Festival cancelled 07/04/2026 Culture French nationals leave Iran after more than three years in detention 07/04/2026 Europe"
